attribute.docString:
Label of the JSON file that contains the RPMs to expose, there's no legacy mode for RPMs defined by a lock file.

The lock file content is as:
```json
    {
        "name": "optional name for the proxy repository, defaults to the file name",
        "cli-arguments": [
            "cli",
            "arguments",
            "used",
            "for"
            "generation",
        ],
        "repositories": {
            "repo-name": [
                "https://repo-url/path",
            ],
        },
        "rpms": [
            {
                "name": "<name of the rpm>",
                "urls": ["<url0>", ...],
                "sha256": "<sha256 of the file>",
                "integrity": "<integrity of the file>"
            }
        ],
        "targets": [
            "target to install",
        ],
        "ignored": [
            "ignored package",
        ],
    }
```
